# Summary of changes for run 6ddcf1c8-8c68-47bb-9259-7f59994f7710
Completed and verified the new research cycle.

Files added:
- `Catalog/Probability/GodelCasinoAsymmetricOdds.lean`
- `FUTURE_DIRECTIONS.md`

The Lean development extends Gödel’s Casino to asymmetric rewards and losses and proves a chained sequence of results:
- closed forms for per-world and prior-weighted randomized payoff;
- formulas for both pure strategies;
- randomized payoff as an affine combination of pure payoffs;
- randomization cannot outperform the better pure strategy;
- a positive randomized edge exists iff a pure strategy has a positive edge;
- under a normalized prior, the sharp break-even thresholds are `a/(a+b)` and `b/(a+b)`;
- profitability occurs exactly outside the resulting no-bet interval;
- abstention guarantees nonnegative value, is optimal when both pure bets are nonpositive, and bounds every randomized strategy.

`FUTURE_DIRECTIONS.md` records concise sanity calculations, explains why sequence/OEIS evidence is inapplicable to this affine problem, and identifies measure-theoretic, sequential, transaction-cost, minimax, and scoring-rule extensions.

The new Lean file compiles independently with `import Mathlib`, contains no `sorry`, `admit`, added axioms, or `implemented_by`, and the principal threshold and abstention theorems use only standard permitted axioms. All work was committed and pushed.
